[[File:map006.png|center|350px]]
'''Stairway to Darkness''' (闇へと続く地下道 ''Yami e to Tsudzuku Chikadō'', '''Underpass to Darkness''') is the 21st sub-chapter of [[Stories of Legend]]. It was added in [[Version 3.2 Update|Version 3.2]] and is available up to {{4c}} difficulty. In [[The Battle Cats Unite!]], it is the 14th sub-chapter in the Stories of Legend and is available up to 3★ difficulty.

==Difficulty==
Stairway to Darkness is not to be underestimated, but it may be easier than [[Silk Road]] depending on what units you have. Ironically, [[Safe & not Sorry|the first stage]] may just be the hardest, due to the volatile combination of [[Pigeon de Sable]] and buffed [[R.Ost]]. The second-hardest stage is probably [[Underground]], which contains three variants of [[Teacher Bun Bun]], making it very difficult to beat without proper [[:Category:Anti-Floating Cats|anti-Floating units]]. The difficulty of the remaining four stages ranges from moderate to fairly difficult.
{{LegendDiff|130|150|130}}

==New Features==
This chapter introduces three new enemies:
*[[Pigeon de Sable]]: A [[:Category:Floating Enemies|Floating]] enemy that has low health and attack power, but possesses a guaranteed chance to produce a level 1 [[Wave Attack]] when it attacks.
*[[Dark Otter]]: A [[:Category:Dark Enemies|Dark]] variant of [[Otta-smack-u]], with improved health, attack power, and an extra knockback, but has slighty slower movement speed than his original variant.
*[[Angelic Sleipnir]]: An [[:Category:Angel Enemies|Angel]] enemy with good range, health, attack power and a very fast attack rate. Angelic Sleipnir also has a small chance to [[Knockback|knockback]] cats, but has slow movement speed.

